<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A({3},\,{-4},\,{-3})</m> and <m>B({7},\,{2},\,{-7})</m>. The point Q divides AB externally in the ratio <m>{3} : {1}</m>.</p><p>Find the position vector of Q.</p><div><m>\overrightarrow{OQ} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Externally, <m>AQ : QB = {3} : {1}</m> with Q on the line AB outside the segment, so <m>\overrightarrow{AQ} = \dfrac{ {3} }{ {3} - {1} }\,\overrightarrow{AB} = {\frac{3}{2}}\,\overrightarrow{AB}</m>. The fraction is greater than 1, so Q is beyond B.</p><p><m>\overrightarrow{AB} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 4 \\ 6 \\ -4 \end{array}\right)}</m>, so <m>\overrightarrow{AQ} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 6 \\ 9 \\ -6 \end{array}\right)}</m> and <m>\overrightarrow{OQ} = \overrightarrow{OA} + \overrightarrow{AQ} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 9 \\ 5 \\ -9 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 9 \\ 5 \\ -9 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>